<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-106) states laws 1-5 with their Lean theorem names and the papers they come from; Sections 4b/4c carry docstrings tying each term to Lewis (2003), Herrgen (2010), Matsuda (2020) Nature and Yamanaka (2023); the math KG loop file registers laws 4-5 with code loci; Lean theorems 4-5 verify. Deductions: the lam_eff weights 0.82/0.18, exponent 0.38, 0.55/0.45 and 0.65/0.35 (L407, L411, L498) have no source and in practice are overridden by observed-period constants (-8); the rosette rate constants (L1073-1074) and the DAPT basal fraction are uncited choices (-4); the kymograph phase_lag exponent 1.4 and amplitude constants are uncited (-2); math KG code loci are section ranges rather than per-equation lines (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L1072–L1074: Rosette rate constants and Hill cue are phenomenological and uncited <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L1072-L1074>",
        "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L402–L416: Unsourced tempo-factor weights/exponents overridden by observed-period constants <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L402-L416>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: the HES7 DDE (L189-294) is the Lewis/Matsuda delayed-autorepression form with separate tau_tx / tau_tl and half-life degradation rates; exact tempo-rescaling invariance is implemented and verified (L297-363); the new lattice (L734-947) couples cells through a delayed neighbour-mean DLL1 signal gating HES7 transcription (Lewis 2003 form, competitive-promoter threshold shift), reduces exactly to a single self-coupled DDE in the in-phase state (Lean theorem 4), and reproduces the delayed-coupling-theory result that in-phase synchrony depends on tau_c / T; DAPT is modelled as loss of NICD (basal promoter) and the washout reset follows. The Matrigel model (L1040-1151) implements an explicit elastic boundary force whose scaling is proven in Lean theorem 5. Deductions: the 6-regime series (L402-416) overrides its own generic formula with per-regime lam_eff values taken from the observed periods, so laws 2-3 are illustrated, not implemented as predictive kinetics (-8); the human regime does not use the vendored Matsuda (2020) human parameters (tau = 51, t_1/2,p = 40 min) but a 2.459x rescaled mouse cell (-4); the coupling gate scales both synthesis and repression threshold by the same factor, a reduction not derived from a promoter model, and tau_c = 0.8 T is chosen for stability rather than measured (-3); the rosette polarisation / epithelialisation rules are phenomenological (-3); the kymograph (L549-599) is a kinematic cosine wave unrelated to the DDE (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L402–L416: Per-regime lam_eff hard-coded from observed periods (human WT = 300/122; LbNOX/azide = (300/122)*(0.41/k_met)); the 6-regime fit is circular <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L402-L416>",
        "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L608–L623: 'Human' cell kinetics = mouse anchor dilated by 300/122 (tau_tx 30.5, tau_tl 13.1, t_1/2,p 38.1 min), not the vendored tau = 51 / t_1/2,p = 40 min <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L608-L623>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — Morphometric validation: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Nine measurements with units and references are emitted by `measure_morphoeval()` (L1256-1368): period ratio 2.4591 vs 2.459, T_human 300.01 vs 300 +/- 18 min, allometry r 0.997, SEM spacing 47.14 px, lattice R 0.85 vs 1.0 ideal (ablated 0.21), T_coll 298.2 vs 300 min, rosette P_rad 0.99 vs 1.0 ideal, Matrigel contrast 1.07 vs 1.0. Deductions: the 6-regime r = 0.9999 / RMSE 2.18 min measurement is circular (the predictions encode the observations, L402-416) (-10); the human period itself is fixed by construction (lam_eff = 300/122) so 300.01 vs 300 validates nothing (-4); the SEM reference value is the script's own output copied into the JSON (-4); the new lattice and rosette references are theoretical ideals (R = 1, P_rad = 1) because the sources report no order parameter (-4); R_post = 0.85 is below the 0.9 line drawn in Panel G and no quantitative resynchronisation time from Matsuda (2020) Nature is compared (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L1298–L1306: 6-regime Pearson r measurement reports a calibration as validation (regimes encode observed periods) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L1298-L1306>",
        "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L1318–L1326: SEM spacing reference_value 47.14 is the script's own measurement <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L1318-L1326>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-6-regime-hes7-genetic-metabolic-perturbation-series-pearson-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-6-species-vertebrate-segmentation-clock-delay-turnover-allometry-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-dll1-notch-coupled-hexagonal-psm-lattice-kuramoto-order-parameter-r-after-dapt-washout-6-cycles>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-human-pluripotent-stem-cell-psm-hes7-achilles-oscillation-period-t-human>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-human-vs-mouse-hes7-segmentation-clock-period-ratio-t-human-t-mouse>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-matrigel-ablation-effect-on-rosette-polarity-order-10-minus-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-matrigel-embedded-10-axioloid-somite-rosette-radial-apical-polarity-order-p-rad>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-post-washout-collective-period-of-the-notch-coupled-lattice-t-coll>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-measurement-vertebrate-somite-psm-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — MorphoEval overall 80.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 closes both v2 remediation items: Section 4b couples the delayed HES7 TTFL to DLL1-Notch delay signalling on a 12 x 12 hexagonal PSM lattice and reproduces the Matsuda (2020) Nature DAPT pulse-washout logic (slow partial synchronisation from random phases, R 0.19 -> 0.40; DAPT collapse; washout reset R ~ 1.00; Notch coupling retains R = 0.85 after 6 cycles vs 0.21 without coupling; collective period 298 min), with Herrgen (2010) coupling-delay and coupling-strength sweeps and an exact mean-field reduction proven in Lean; Section 4c adds a Matrigel elastic boundary force to a reduced 2D rosette model that epithelialises only when embedded (P_rad -0.08 -> 0.99 from 0 % to 10 % Matrigel, Spearman rho 0.94). The overall score nevertheless falls from 91.7 to 80.0 because the re-audit exposed that the 6-regime perturbation series is calibrated to the observed periods it is scored against (r = 0.9999 is circular), the 'human' cell is a rescaled mouse cell rather than the vendored Matsuda (2020) human kinetics, the kymograph is kinematic, the specimen is a chick SEM with a self-referential reference value, and two CLI parameters are dead. Those defects are now carried explicitly as Pass 4 remediation items. Overall 80.0/100 (faithfulness 76.4, reproducibility 88.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/human_somite_organoid_clock_comparison.png: rendered output of 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py at d58a084, image/png, 1774211 B, 2775×2430 px, artifact_sha256 9f51f92b46d6a341eea40af3bf94cfb9d643809033460182d5d2873b9bd4c2d2 (sha256 9f51f92b46d6a341eea40af3bf94cfb9d643809033460182d5d2873b9bd4c2d2), spec_fingerprint dc5fc9fc0d0a3efa51f3e2df8dff0c42308ff7921502f484af6294b4b564fb24. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dc5fc9fc0d0a3efa51f3e2df8dff0c42308ff7921502f484af6294b4b564fb24; artifact_sha256: 9f51f92b46d6a341eea40af3bf94cfb9d643809033460182d5d2873b9bd4c2d2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json=b045a3f334ced9d4..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/scout_manifest.json=a3af01b1b2956954...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-human-somite-organoid-clock-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118: ~5.0 h (300 +/- 18 min) HES7-Achilles oscillations in human pluripotent stem-cell-derived presomitic mesoderm vs ~2.0 h (122 min) in mouse PSM | Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455: species-specific HES7 intron splicing delay and protein/mRNA half-lives, not the hHES7 locus sequence, govern the ~2.5x human slowdown; intronless Hes7 abolishes oscillations | Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Nature 613:550-557: mitochondrial ETC activity and cytosolic NAD+/NADH modulate translation rate and clock period (LbNOX acceleration ~228 min, azide/rotenone slowdown ~402 min) | Matsuda et al. (2020) Nature 580:124-129: a DAPT pulse followed by washout synchronises HES7 oscillations across hPSC-derived PSM cultures; Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science: Notch inhibition desynchronises segmentation clock cells; Herrgen et al. (2010) Curr. Biol.: delayed intercellular coupling sets the collective period | Yamanaka et al. (2023) Nature 614:509-520 and Sanaki-Matsumiya et al. (2022) Nat. Commun. 13:2325: epithelial somite rosettes form only in Matrigel-embedded human axioloids / somitoids (qualitative); reconstructed_in_script: Delayed autoinhibitory HES7 TTFL RK2 DDE solver (mouse WT 122.00 min; rescaled 'human' cell 300.01 min), exact tempo-rescaling collapse across lambda in [1, 3] (max std 2.32e-13 nM), intronless-Hes7 subcritical collapse, and a 6-regime series whose per-regime tempo factors are hard-coded from the observed periods (Pearson r = 0.9999 is a calibration, not a prediction) | 6-species vertebrate clock allometry (r = 0.9970) from a vendored species table of delays/half-lives, a kinematic (not DDE-derived) axioloid phase-wave kymograph, and bilateral DoG somite segmentation on a chick embryo SEM (47.14 px mean spacing, CV 0.2010) | Pass 3: DLL1-Notch delay-coupled HES7 lattice (12 x 12 hex, eps = 0.25, tau_c = 0.8 T, 5 % tempo CV) through the DAPT pulse-washout protocol: R_0 = 0.19 -> R_pre = 0.40 after 5 coupled cycles; DAPT amplitude ratio 0.17; washout reset R = 0.9995; R retained after 6 cycles = 0.85 (coupled) vs 0.21 (coupling-ablated, lost at 3.0 cycles); T_coll = 298.2 min; in-phase stable for tau_c/T in [0.625, 0.95]; T_coll(tau_c) spans 235-417 min; R_end(eps) 0.26 -> 0.96 (eps 0 -> 0.25), 0.88 at 0.35 | Pass 3: reduced 2D cell-centre Matrigel rosette model: P_rad = -0.08 (0 %) -> 0.99 (10 %), epithelial fraction 0 -> 0.67, aggregate radius 85 -> 28 um, Matrigel sweep Spearman rho = 0.94; transfer_boundary: Single-cell / lattice HES7 DDE kinetics are compared with a chick (Gallus gallus) dorsal SEM, not with a human axioloid image; the 47.14 px 'reference' spacing is the script's own measurement recorded in the dataset JSON | tau_c = 0.8 T (240 min) is an assumption from delayed-coupling-theory stability, not a human measurement; the DAPT basal promoter fraction b = 0.1 and the competitive-promoter gate (synthesis and threshold both scaled by (1 - eps) + 2 eps S) are modelling reductions | Matrigel stiffness kappa = 0.01 min^-1 per % and the polarisation / constriction rate constants are phenomenological; the rosette reference values (P_rad = 1, contrast = 1) are geometric ideals, not measured organoid morphometrics; does_not_claim: Prediction of the LbNOX / azide / hHES7-swap periods from independently measured kinetics (they are encoded); 3D actomyosin apical-constriction FEM; Matrigel rheology; measured human Notch coupling delay; Floquet/stability analysis of the coupled DDE beyond the numerical lattice scan." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:1034-1074 — kappa = 0.01 min^-1 per % Matrigel, phi_half = 4 %, and the rosette rate constants are phenomenological. Calibrate kappa to published Matrigel storage moduli versus concentration, extend the rosette to a multi-cell-layer ring with a lumen (or a 2D vertex model) and add a quantitative morphometric (rosette diameter, cell aspect ratio) comparable to axioloid somite sizes.",
        "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:1733-1825 — the GIF still shows only the single-cell traces and the kinematic wavefront; add the lattice phase map through the DAPT protocol and the rosette relaxation so the animated artifact reflects the Pass 3 model, and vendor a requirements lock for this script.",
        "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:402-416 — `evaluate_perturbation_series` overrides its generic lam_eff with observed-period constants (human WT = 300/122; LbNOX/azide = (300/122)*(0.41/k_met)) and the JSON k_met values (0.54, 0.31) are themselves 0.41*300/T_obs, so Pearson r = 0.9999 (measurement L1298-1307) is circular. Replace with a single predictive mapping from the vendored per-regime (tau_total, t_half_p, t_half_m, k_met) to DDE parameters (e.g. tau_i = tau_total * split, delta = ln2/t_half, alpha scaled by k_met) fitted on mouse WT only, report the out-of-sample RMSE for the other five regimes honestly, and drop the regime-specific branches.",
        "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:549-599 — `simulate_axioloid_kymograph` is a prescribed cos(omega t - phase_lag(x)) wave with hand-set somite boundaries. Derive the kymograph from the Notch-coupled lattice (Section 4b) with an anteroposterior gradient of cell-autonomous period (or a moving determination front that freezes cells), so Panel D is model output and somite size S = v_wf * T is emergent.",
        "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:608-623 and 1288-1297 — the 'human' cell is the mouse anchor dilated by 300/122 (tau_tx 30.5, tau_tl 13.1, t_1/2,p 38.1, t_1/2,m 35.9 min), not the vendored Matsuda (2020) human kinetics (tau = 51, t_1/2,p = 40, t_1/2,m = 42 min, JSON L123-140). Run the human regime and the Notch lattice from the measured human parameters (re-tuning alpha/K/n once), so that the 300 min period is a prediction rather than a construction, and wire `--tau-human` / `--thalf-human` (L1931-1932, currently dead) into that run.",
        "remediation needed: 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py:836-837 and 143 — the Notch gate scales synthesis and repression threshold by the same factor and tau_c = 0.8 T is chosen from the stability scan. Derive the gate from an explicit competitive NICD/RBPJ vs HES7 promoter-occupancy model, and sweep tau_c jointly with eps to map the Arnold-tongue-like stability region (Panel H currently shows a single eps slice); report R_end(eps) beyond 0.25 where it becomes non-monotone (0.88 at 0.35).",
        "remediation needed: datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json:56-90 and script 1318-1327 — the specimen is a chick embryo SEM and its reference spacing (47.14 px) is the script's own output. Vendor a CC-licensed human axioloid / somitoid image (e.g. from the Yamanaka 2023 or Sanaki-Matsumiya 2022 open supplementary data) or a digitised somite-size table from those papers, and compare the rosette model's aggregate radius (28 um at 10 %) and the lattice somite size against it." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Four parameters now visibly control the form they should: lambda dilates the period exactly linearly (L297-363); Notch coupling strength eps raises retained synchrony 0.26 -> 0.96 over 0 -> 0.25 (L961-987); the coupling delay tau_c/T switches in-phase stability off below ~0.6 and on above it and modulates the collective period 235 -> 417 min (L989-1027); the Matrigel fraction raises rosette polarity monotonically (Spearman rho 0.94) and shrinks the aggregate 85 -> 28 um (L1153-1176). Deductions: `--tau-human` and `--thalf-human` are parsed but never used (L1931-1932) (-6); the 6 regimes and 6 species are not swept parameters but hard-coded tempo factors (L402-416, L498) (-6); R_end(eps) is non-monotone at eps = 0.35 (0.88 < 0.96), so the stated monotone control holds only up to 0.25 (-2); pre-DAPT synchronisation from random phases reaches only R = 0.40 in 5 cycles, and the lattice size / heterogeneity are not swept (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L1931–L1936: --tau-human / --thalf-human are never read (dead parameters); --eps-notch / --tau-c-fraction / --matrigel-pct do drive an extra run <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L1931-L1936>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic (seed 2019) with bitwise two-run checks for the kymograph, the lattice R(t) and the rosette positions; `--self-test` runs 8 blocks in ~14 s and the default render completes in ~17 s; all three media outputs are regenerated by the default invocation; new CLI flags are documented in argparse; the environment is recorded here. Deductions: no requirements lock file is vendored for this script (-4); two dead CLI parameters remain (-3); without MPLCONFIGDIR matplotlib emits a cache warning in this environment (-2); the GIF does not include the new lattice/rosette dynamics (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
