    dct:description "Nine primary sources with DOIs in the docstring, dataset README, BibTeX and reference JSON; the five Pass 3 DOIs and author lists were resolved against Crossref; the specimen and scout manifest are SHA-256 pinned and verified at every run (L145-176); the reference JSON records the Notch-lattice and Matrigel parameter tables with their empirical anchors and caveats (JSON L273-375). Deductions: the reference JSON digest is recomputed but not pinned, so silent edits to the kinetic tables would pass verification (-3); the specimen licence/URL is traceable but it is a chick SEM standing in for a human organoid (-3); the Herrgen tau_c anchor is zebrafish and is only qualitatively transferred (-2)." ;
