<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — Morphological realism / specimen match: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Judged on the regenerated PNGs: Panel E overlays the detected bilateral somite rows on the SEM and the periodicity is visibly matched (Panel F waveform r = 0.48); the new lattice figure shows the expected phenomenology (incoherent -> partially clustered -> collapsed -> reset -> coupled lattice stays ordered while the ablated one scrambles), and Panel I shows a compact radially polarised rosette inside the Matrigel shell against a dispersed unpolarised 0 % aggregate. Deductions: the specimen is a chick embryo SEM (dataset JSON L60), not a human axioloid or any figure from the four source papers, so the human organoid morphology itself is never compared (-12); the rosette and lattice panels are compared with no side-by-side image from Yamanaka (2023) / Matsuda (2020) Nature (-8); the kymograph (Panel D) is a hand-drawn kinematic wave (-4); the rosette is a 24-cell 2D cross-section without a lumen or the multi-somite periodic array of the axioloid (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py L549–L599: Axioloid kymograph is a prescribed cos(omega t - phase_lag(x)) wave with hand-set somite boundaries, not DDE output <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L549-L599>",
        "datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json L56–L89: Specimen is Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo' (chick, not human organoid); empirical_somite_metrics are the script's own outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json#L56-L89>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

