<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) & Matsuda et al. (2020) HES7 Delay-Degradation Tempo Rescaling Invariance Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that concerted scaling of HES7 feedback delay tau and protein/mRNA half-lives dilates the segmentation clock period by exact factor lambda (~2.5x from mouse 120 min to human 300 min) | Variables: T_osc: HES7 segmentation clock oscillation period (min); lambda: biochemical delay and half-life dilation factor (dimensionless, ~2.5 between human and mouse); tau: total transcriptional-splicing + translational feedback delay (min); delta: mRNA/protein degradation rate (min^-1)" ;
    dct:source "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118 Fig. 2; Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L120-L245>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L25-L53> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def scaled_clock_period (lambda T0 : Nat) : Nat :=
  lambda * T0
theorem diazcuadros_matsuda_2020_tempo_rescaling_invariance
    (lambda lambda1 lambda2 T0 T1 T2 : Nat) :
    scaled_clock_period lambda1 (scaled_clock_period lambda2 T0) =
      scaled_clock_period (lambda1 * lambda2) T0 ∧
    scaled_clock_period lambda (T1 + T2) =
      scaled_clock_period lambda T1 + scaled_clock_period lambda T2 ∧
    scaled_clock_period 5 60 = 300"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_osc(lambda * tau, delta / lambda) = lambda * T_osc(tau, delta),  with lambda_human_mouse = 300 / 120 = 2.5" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.scaled_clock_period" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.diazcuadros_matsuda_2020_tempo_rescaling_invariance" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Matsuda et al. (2020) Intron-Splicing Delay Decomposition & Subcritical Hopf Oscillation Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that HES7 intron splicing delay is required to maintain total feedback delay above the Hopf bifurcation threshold tau_crit, explaining why intronless Hes7 abolishes segmentation clock oscillations | Variables: tau_intron: HES7 pre-mRNA intron splicing delay (15 min in mouse, 37 min in human); tau_tl: basal export and translation delay (min); tau_crit: minimum feedback delay required for sustained Hopf limit-cycle oscillations (min)" ;
    dct:source "Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L248-L335>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L55-L84> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wt_total_delay (tau_intron tau_tl : Nat) : Nat :=
  tau_intron + tau_tl
def intronless_delay (tau_tl : Nat) : Nat :=
  tau_tl
theorem matsuda_2020_intron_deletion_delay_shortening
    (tau_intron tau_tl tau_crit : Nat)
    (h_intron : 0 < tau_intron)
    (h_sub : tau_tl < tau_crit)
    (h_super : tau_crit ≤ tau_intron + tau_tl) :
    intronless_delay tau_tl < wt_total_delay tau_intron tau_tl ∧
    intronless_delay tau_tl < tau_crit ∧
    tau_crit ≤ wt_total_delay tau_intron tau_tl"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "tau_WT = tau_intron + tau_tl > tau_crit > tau_tl = tau_Delta_intron  =>  damped steady-state collapse" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.wt_total_delay" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.matsuda_2020_intron_deletion_delay_shortening" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Mitochondrial NAD+/NADH Metabolic Rate Scaling Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that mitochondrial electron transport chain inhibition (k_ETC < k_WT) slows the human segmentation clock whereas LbNOX-mediated NAD+/NADH elevation (k_LbNOX > k_WT) accelerates clock frequency and shortens period | Variables: k_met: NAD+/NADH-dependent translation and protein turnover rate factor; T_osc: HES7 oscillation period (min); omega_osc: clock angular frequency (rad/min)" ;
    dct:source "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Nature 613:550-557 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L338-L445>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L86-L119> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def metabolic_phase_cycle_residual (k_met T_osc C_cycle : Int) : Int :=
  k_met * T_osc - C_cycle
def metabolic_clock_frequency (k_met omega_base : Int) : Int :=
  k_met * omega_base
theorem diazcuadros_2023_metabolic_nad_period_scaling
    (k_met q k_etc k_wt k_lbnox omega_base : Int)
    (h_etc_wt : k_etc < k_wt)
    (h_wt_lbnox : k_wt < k_lbnox)
    (h_omega : 0 < omega_base) :
    metabolic_phase_cycle_residual k_met q (k_met * q) = 0 ∧
    metabolic_clock_frequency k_etc omega_base < metabolic_clock_frequency k_wt omega_base ∧
    metabolic_clock_frequency k_wt omega_base < metabolic_clock_frequency k_lbnox omega_base"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_met * T_osc = C_cycle,  omega_osc(k_ETC) < omega_osc(k_WT) < omega_osc(k_LbNOX)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.metabolic_phase_cycle_residual" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.diazcuadros_2023_metabolic_nad_period_scaling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lewis (2003) / Herrgen et al. (2010) DLL1-Notch Delay Coupling Mean-Field Reduction & DAPT Gating Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Couples the single-cell HES7 TTFL to its hexagonal neighbours through delayed DLL1-Notch signalling; proves the synchronised lattice reduces exactly to one self-coupled DDE (so the collective period T_coll(tau_c) is a single-cell computation, Herrgen 2010), that the lattice has 3N edges, and that DAPT strictly lowers HES7 synthesis below the uncoupled rate (oscillation collapse before washout re-synchronisation, Matsuda 2020 Nature) | Variables: D_i: DLL1 ligand level of cell i (nM); k_i <= 6: number of hexagonal neighbours; tau_c: intercellular Notch coupling delay (min, default 0.8 T); S_i: NICD activation (dimensionless); eps: coupling modulation depth (0.25); K_D: Notch half-activation (nM, calibrated to <D> over one cycle); b: Notch-independent basal HES7 promoter activity under DAPT (0.1)" ;
    dct:source "Lewis (2003) Curr. Biol. 13:1398-1408; Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science 317:1911-1915; Herrgen et al. (2010) Curr. Biol. 20:1244-1253; Matsuda et al. (2020) Nature 580:124-129; Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L601-L1027>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L121-L173> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def neighbour_mean_delta (k d : Nat) : Nat :=
  (k * d) / k
def hex_lattice_edge_count (n : Nat) : Nat :=
  (6 * n) / 2
def notch_gated_synthesis (alpha eps s2 : Nat) : Nat :=
  alpha * (100 - eps + eps * s2 / 100)
theorem lewis_herrgen_notch_coupling_mean_field_dapt_gating
    (k d n alpha eps : Nat)
    (h_k : 0 < k)
    (h_alpha : 0 < alpha)
    (h_eps_pos : 0 < eps)
    (h_eps_le : eps ≤ 100) :
    neighbour_mean_delta k d = d ∧
    hex_lattice_edge_count n = 3 * n ∧
    notch_gated_synthesis alpha eps 100 = alpha * 100 ∧
    notch_gated_synthesis alpha eps 0 < notch_gated_synthesis alpha eps 100"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "D_bar_i(t) = (1/k_i) sum_{j in N6(i)} D_j(t);  S_i = D_bar_i(t - tau_c)^h / (K_D^h + D_bar_i(t - tau_c)^h);  dm_i/dt = alpha_m [(1 - eps) + 2 eps S_i] / (1 + (p_i(t - tau_tx,i) / (K [(1 - eps) + 2 eps S_i]))^n) - delta_m,i m_i;  in-phase state: k D / k = D  =>  single self-coupled DDE;  DAPT: S_i = 0 => synthesis b alpha_m < alpha_m" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.neighbour_mean_delta" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.lewis_herrgen_notch_coupling_mean_field_dapt_gating" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023) Matrigel-Embedded Elastic Boundary Force Scaling Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Makes the Matrigel embedding an explicit mechanical boundary force in the reduced axioloid rosette model: no force without Matrigel or inside the shell, and strictly stronger confinement with Matrigel fraction, which together with the ECM-contact polarity cue produces the epithelial rosette only in embedded aggregates (Yamanaka 2023; Sanaki-Matsumiya 2022) | Variables: phi: Matrigel volume fraction (%); kappa: shell stiffness per % Matrigel (0.01 min^-1 per %, uncalibrated); R_M: ECM shell radius (28 um); x_i, c: cell centre and aggregate centroid (um); r_hat_i: outward radial unit vector" ;
    dct:source "Yamanaka et al. (2023) Nature 614:509-520; Sanaki-Matsumiya et al. (2022) Nat. Commun. 13:2325" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L1029-L1176>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L175-L212> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def matrigel_stiffness (kappa phi : Nat) : Nat :=
  kappa * phi
def matrigel_boundary_force (kappa phi r R : Nat) : Nat :=
  matrigel_stiffness kappa phi * (r - R)
theorem yamanaka_2023_matrigel_boundary_force_scaling
    (kappa phi phi1 phi2 r_in r_out R : Nat)
    (h_kappa : 0 < kappa)
    (h_inside : r_in ≤ R)
    (h_outside : R < r_out)
    (h_phi : phi1 < phi2) :
    matrigel_boundary_force kappa 0 r_out R = 0 ∧
    matrigel_boundary_force kappa phi r_in R = 0 ∧
    matrigel_boundary_force kappa phi1 r_out R < matrigel_boundary_force kappa phi2 r_out R"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_M(phi) = kappa * phi;  F_M,i = -k_M(phi) * max(0, |x_i - c| - R_M) * r_hat_i;  F_M(phi = 0) = 0;  F_M(|x_i - c| <= R_M) = 0;  phi1 < phi2 => |F_M(phi1)| < |F_M(phi2)| outside the shell" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.matrigel_boundary_force" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.yamanaka_2023_matrigel_boundary_force_scaling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) & Matsuda et al. (2020) HES7 Delay-Degradation Tempo Rescaling Invariance Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that concerted scaling of HES7 feedback delay tau and protein/mRNA half-lives dilates the segmentation clock period by exact factor lambda (~2.5x from mouse 120 min to human 300 min) | Variables: T_osc: HES7 segmentation clock oscillation period (min); lambda: biochemical delay and half-life dilation factor (dimensionless, ~2.5 between human and mouse); tau: total transcriptional-splicing + translational feedback delay (min); delta: mRNA/protein degradation rate (min^-1)" ;
    dct:source "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118 Fig. 2; Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L120-L245>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L25-L53> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def scaled_clock_period (lambda T0 : Nat) : Nat :=
  lambda * T0
theorem diazcuadros_matsuda_2020_tempo_rescaling_invariance
    (lambda lambda1 lambda2 T0 T1 T2 : Nat) :
    scaled_clock_period lambda1 (scaled_clock_period lambda2 T0) =
      scaled_clock_period (lambda1 * lambda2) T0 ∧
    scaled_clock_period lambda (T1 + T2) =
      scaled_clock_period lambda T1 + scaled_clock_period lambda T2 ∧
    scaled_clock_period 5 60 = 300"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "T_osc(lambda * tau, delta / lambda) = lambda * T_osc(tau, delta),  with lambda_human_mouse = 300 / 120 = 2.5" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.scaled_clock_period" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.diazcuadros_matsuda_2020_tempo_rescaling_invariance" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Matsuda et al. (2020) Intron-Splicing Delay Decomposition & Subcritical Hopf Oscillation Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that HES7 intron splicing delay is required to maintain total feedback delay above the Hopf bifurcation threshold tau_crit, explaining why intronless Hes7 abolishes segmentation clock oscillations | Variables: tau_intron: HES7 pre-mRNA intron splicing delay (15 min in mouse, 37 min in human); tau_tl: basal export and translation delay (min); tau_crit: minimum feedback delay required for sustained Hopf limit-cycle oscillations (min)" ;
    dct:source "Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L248-L335>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L55-L84> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wt_total_delay (tau_intron tau_tl : Nat) : Nat :=
  tau_intron + tau_tl
def intronless_delay (tau_tl : Nat) : Nat :=
  tau_tl
theorem matsuda_2020_intron_deletion_delay_shortening
    (tau_intron tau_tl tau_crit : Nat)
    (h_intron : 0 < tau_intron)
    (h_sub : tau_tl < tau_crit)
    (h_super : tau_crit ≤ tau_intron + tau_tl) :
    intronless_delay tau_tl < wt_total_delay tau_intron tau_tl ∧
    intronless_delay tau_tl < tau_crit ∧
    tau_crit ≤ wt_total_delay tau_intron tau_tl"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "tau_WT = tau_intron + tau_tl > tau_crit > tau_tl = tau_Delta_intron  =>  damped steady-state collapse" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.wt_total_delay" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.matsuda_2020_intron_deletion_delay_shortening" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Mitochondrial NAD+/NADH Metabolic Rate Scaling Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that mitochondrial electron transport chain inhibition (k_ETC < k_WT) slows the human segmentation clock whereas LbNOX-mediated NAD+/NADH elevation (k_LbNOX > k_WT) accelerates clock frequency and shortens period | Variables: k_met: NAD+/NADH-dependent translation and protein turnover rate factor; T_osc: HES7 oscillation period (min); omega_osc: clock angular frequency (rad/min)" ;
    dct:source "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Nature 613:550-557 Figs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py#L338-L445>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean#L86-L119> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def metabolic_phase_cycle_residual (k_met T_osc C_cycle : Int) : Int :=
  k_met * T_osc - C_cycle
def metabolic_clock_frequency (k_met omega_base : Int) : Int :=
  k_met * omega_base
theorem diazcuadros_2023_metabolic_nad_period_scaling
    (k_met q k_etc k_wt k_lbnox omega_base : Int)
    (h_etc_wt : k_etc < k_wt)
    (h_wt_lbnox : k_wt < k_lbnox)
    (h_omega : 0 < omega_base) :
    metabolic_phase_cycle_residual k_met q (k_met * q) = 0 ∧
    metabolic_clock_frequency k_etc omega_base < metabolic_clock_frequency k_wt omega_base ∧
    metabolic_clock_frequency k_wt omega_base < metabolic_clock_frequency k_lbnox omega_base"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_met * T_osc = C_cycle,  omega_osc(k_ETC) < omega_osc(k_WT) < omega_osc(k_LbNOX)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1885-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2144-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05574-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05649-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1142538>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aba7668> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Delayed Autoinhibitory HES7 Oscillator with Intron Splicing Delay & NAD+/NADH Metabolic Tempo Scaling" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.metabolic_phase_cycle_residual" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_028.diazcuadros_2023_metabolic_nad_period_scaling" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

